### Target.attachToTarget

Source: https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target

Attaches to the target with the given ID. Optionally enables flat access to the session.

```APIDOC
## Target.attachToTarget

### Description
Attaches to the target with the given ID. Optionally enables flat access to the session.

### Method
POST

### Endpoint
/json/version

### Parameters
#### Path Parameters
None

#### Query Parameters
None

#### Request Body
- **targetId** (TargetID) - Required - The ID of the target to attach to.
- **flatten** (boolean) - Optional - Enables "flat" access to the session. Defaults to false.

### Request Example
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "method": "Target.attachToTarget",
  "params": {
    "targetId": "TARGET_ID",
    "flatten": true
  }
}
```

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **sessionId** (SessionID) - The ID assigned to the session.

#### Response Example
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "result": {
    "sessionId": "SESSION_ID"
  }
}
```
```

--------------------------------

### Target.sendMessageToTarget

Source: https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target

Sends protocol message over session with given id. Deprecated, consider using flat mode instead.

```APIDOC
## Target.sendMessageToTarget

### Description
Sends protocol message over session with given id. Consider using flat mode instead; see commands attachToTarget, setAutoAttach, and crbug.com/991325.

### Method
POST

### Endpoint
/json/protocol/Target.sendMessageToTarget

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **message** (string) - Required
- **sessionId** (SessionID) - Required - Identifier of the session.
- **targetId** (TargetID) - Deprecated - Deprecated.

### Request Example
{
  "message": "{\"id\": 1, \"method\": \"Page.enable\"}",
  "sessionId": "12345"
}
```
